{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-solid"},{"type":"text","value":". Import the UI factory from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-solid/ui"},{"type":"text","value":". Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatHook({ options, ...components })"},{"type":"text","value":" once at module scope. Your app calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAppChat()"},{"type":"text","value":" to create the instance. Render "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<chat.AppChat />"},{"type":"text","value":". Do not destructure reactive props."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecated."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Do not install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-solid-ui"},{"type":"text","value":". That package re-exports this subpath until 1.0.0. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../migration/create-ui","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat UI packages"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The factory needs a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":" entry for every tool name in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatOptions"},{"type":"text","value":". It also needs an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents.generic"},{"type":"text","value":" entry for every interrupt id. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generic.fallback"},{"type":"text","value":" is optional. Widgets go in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"components"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":", the same way Form and Table register components."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server route matches the "},{"type":"link","href":"./react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React page"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-5.6"},{"type":"text","value":" on the OpenAI text adapter."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"./recipes/index","children":[{"type":"text","value":"chat UI recipes"}]},{"type":"text","value":" show the same option groups one at a time. The code there is React, and the shape carries over."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createSignal } from 'solid-js'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-solid/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat, useChatContext } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n  layout: (props) => (\n    <>\n      <props.Messages />\n      <props.Interrupts />\n      <props.Queue />\n      <props.Input />\n    </>\n  ),\n  input: () => {\n    const chat = useChatContext()\n    const [draft, setDraft] = createSignal('')\n    return (\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault()\n          void chat.sendMessage(draft())\n          setDraft('')\n        }}\n      >\n        <input onInput={(event) => setDraft(event.currentTarget.value)} value={draft()} />\n        <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n      </form>\n    )\n  },\n  message: (props) => <article><props.Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: {\n  fallback: (props) => <span>{props.part.type}</span>,\n  },\n  toolsComponents: {\n  getWeather: (props) => <strong>{props.part.input?.city}</strong>,\n  },\n})\n\nexport function Support() {\n  const chat = useAppChat({ threadId: 'support-1' })\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layout"},{"type":"text","value":" receives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.Messages"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.Interrupts"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.Input"},{"type":"text","value":" as components. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Input"},{"type":"text","value":" is only present when the config registers an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"List "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input"},{"type":"text","value":" before "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layout"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"text","value":" An inline "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"function"},{"type":"text","value":" expression written "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"after"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layout"},{"type":"text","value":" stops TypeScript inferring that an input is registered, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Input"},{"type":"text","value":" goes missing from the layout props. Putting "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input"},{"type":"text","value":" first fixes it, as does an arrow or a named reference. If it slips through, rendering "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<props.Input />"},{"type":"text","value":" without a registered "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input"},{"type":"text","value":" warns once in development."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-a-component-in-its-own-file","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type a component in its own file"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolProps"},{"type":"text","value":" the same way as React. Keep the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props"},{"type":"text","value":" object so Solid can track it."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\nimport { createChatHook, type ToolProps } from '@tanstack/ai-solid/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nexport function WeatherTool(\n  props: ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'>,\n) {\n  return <strong>{props.part.input?.city}</strong>\n}\n\nexport const { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: (props) => <props.Messages />,\n    message: (props) => <article><props.Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: { fallback: () => null },\n  toolsComponents: { getWeather: WeatherTool },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Part components use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PartProps<typeof chatOptions, 'text'>"},{"type":"text","value":". Then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part"},{"type":"text","value":" is already a text part."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interrupt components use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InterruptProps<typeof chatOptions, 'choosePlan'>"},{"type":"text","value":". Then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt.payload"},{"type":"text","value":" matches the definition."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mapped components do not receive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat"},{"type":"text","value":" as a prop. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChatContext()"},{"type":"text","value":" when a component needs live chat. That call opts the component into chat updates. Nested children can call it too."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"read-chat-from-usechatcontext","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read chat from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChatContext()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-solid/ui'\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n}\n\nfunction StatusLine() {\n  const chat = useChatContext()\n  return <p>{chat.messages.length} messages</p>\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat, useChatContext } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: (props) => (\n      <>\n        <StatusLine />\n        <props.Messages />\n      </>\n    ),\n    message: (props) => <article><props.Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: { fallback: () => null },\n})\n\nexport function ChatScreen() {\n  const chat = useAppChat()\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChatContext()"},{"type":"text","value":" only inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AppChat"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Provider"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"interrupts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interrupts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool approvals sit in the tool when you read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.interrupt"},{"type":"text","value":". Put a component on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents.tools"},{"type":"text","value":" to send that approval to the list instead. Generic interrupts always sit in the list under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents.generic"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ choosePlan, fallback }"},{"type":"text","value":". An unbound interrupt uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fallback"},{"type":"text","value":". Branch on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt.kind === 'unbound'"},{"type":"text","value":" if the copy must differ."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The full map is on the "},{"type":"link","href":"./react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React page"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual list: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<UI.Messages>{(messages) => <span>{messages().length}</span>}</UI.Messages>"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.chat"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.part"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.Parts"},{"type":"text","value":" without destructure."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"render-markdown","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render markdown"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model replies arrive as markdown. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TextPart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-solid/ui"},{"type":"text","value":" renders it with "},{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/markdown","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Markdown"}]},{"type":"text","value":". By default, raw HTML is escaped and executable URLs are removed."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { TextPart } from '@tanstack/ai-solid/ui'\n\nexport function Reply(props: { content: string }) {\n  return <TextPart content={props.content} />\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fenced code stays plain until you pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"highlighter"},{"type":"text","value":". Build one with TanStack Highlight: "},{"type":"link","href":"./markdown","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Highlight markdown code"}]},{"type":"text","value":". A custom "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"highlighter"},{"type":"text","value":" returns trusted HTML. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTanStackMarkdownHighlighter"},{"type":"text","value":", or another highlighter that escapes source text."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"highlighter"},{"type":"text","value":": a synchronous "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CodeHighlighter"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"extensions"},{"type":"text","value":": extra TanStack Markdown extensions. The streaming extension is always on."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you still pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"remarkPlugins"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rehypePlugins"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"disableDefaultPlugins"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"components"},{"type":"text","value":", see "},{"type":"link","href":"../migration/text-part-markdown","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TextPart markdown"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"client","text":"Client","level":2},{"id":"type-a-component-in-its-own-file","text":"Type a component in its own file","level":2},{"id":"read-chat-from-usechatcontext","text":"Read chat from useChatContext()","level":2},{"id":"interrupts","text":"Interrupts","level":2},{"id":"render-markdown","text":"Render markdown","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nInstall `@tanstack/ai-solid`. Import the UI factory from `@tanstack/ai-solid/ui`. Call `createChatHook({ options, ...components })` once at module scope. Your app calls `useAppChat()` to create the instance. Render `<chat.AppChat />`. Do not destructure reactive props.\n\n> **Deprecated.** Do not install `@tanstack/ai-solid-ui`. That package re-exports this subpath until 1.0.0. See [Chat UI packages](../migration/create-ui).\n\nThe factory needs a `toolsComponents` entry for every tool name in `chatOptions`. It also needs an `interruptsComponents.generic` entry for every interrupt id. `generic.fallback` is optional. Widgets go in `components`, `partsComponents`, `toolsComponents`, and `interruptsComponents`, the same way Form and Table register components.\n\nThe server route matches the [React page](./react). Use `gpt-5.6` on the OpenAI text adapter.\n\nThe [chat UI recipes](./recipes/index) show the same option groups one at a time. The code there is React, and the shape carries over.\n\n## Client\n\n```tsx\nimport { createSignal } from 'solid-js'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-solid/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat, useChatContext } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n  layout: (props) => (\n    <>\n      <props.Messages />\n      <props.Interrupts />\n      <props.Queue />\n      <props.Input />\n    </>\n  ),\n  input: () => {\n    const chat = useChatContext()\n    const [draft, setDraft] = createSignal('')\n    return (\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault()\n          void chat.sendMessage(draft())\n          setDraft('')\n        }}\n      >\n        <input onInput={(event) => setDraft(event.currentTarget.value)} value={draft()} />\n        <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n      </form>\n    )\n  },\n  message: (props) => <article><props.Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: {\n  fallback: (props) => <span>{props.part.type}</span>,\n  },\n  toolsComponents: {\n  getWeather: (props) => <strong>{props.part.input?.city}</strong>,\n  },\n})\n\nexport function Support() {\n  const chat = useAppChat({ threadId: 'support-1' })\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}\n```\n\n`layout` receives `props.Messages`, `props.Interrupts`, and `props.Input` as components. `Input` is only present when the config registers an `input`.\n\n> **List `input` before `layout`.** An inline `function` expression written *after* `layout` stops TypeScript inferring that an input is registered, and `Input` goes missing from the layout props. Putting `input` first fixes it, as does an arrow or a named reference. If it slips through, rendering `<props.Input />` without a registered `input` warns once in development.\n\n## Type a component in its own file\n\nUse `ToolProps` the same way as React. Keep the `props` object so Solid can track it.\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\nimport { createChatHook, type ToolProps } from '@tanstack/ai-solid/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nexport function WeatherTool(\n  props: ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'>,\n) {\n  return <strong>{props.part.input?.city}</strong>\n}\n\nexport const { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: (props) => <props.Messages />,\n    message: (props) => <article><props.Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: { fallback: () => null },\n  toolsComponents: { getWeather: WeatherTool },\n})\n```\n\nPart components use `PartProps<typeof chatOptions, 'text'>`. Then `part` is already a text part.\n\nInterrupt components use `InterruptProps<typeof chatOptions, 'choosePlan'>`. Then `interrupt.payload` matches the definition.\n\nMapped components do not receive `chat` as a prop. Call `useChatContext()` when a component needs live chat. That call opts the component into chat updates. Nested children can call it too.\n\n## Read chat from `useChatContext()`\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-solid/ui'\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n}\n\nfunction StatusLine() {\n  const chat = useChatContext()\n  return <p>{chat.messages.length} messages</p>\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat, useChatContext } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: (props) => (\n      <>\n        <StatusLine />\n        <props.Messages />\n      </>\n    ),\n    message: (props) => <article><props.Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: { fallback: () => null },\n})\n\nexport function ChatScreen() {\n  const chat = useAppChat()\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}\n```\n\nCall `useChatContext()` only inside `AppChat` or `Provider`.\n\n## Interrupts\n\nTool approvals sit in the tool when you read `props.interrupt`. Put a component on `interruptsComponents.tools` to send that approval to the list instead. Generic interrupts always sit in the list under `interruptsComponents.generic`: `{ choosePlan, fallback }`. An unbound interrupt uses `fallback`. Branch on `interrupt.kind === 'unbound'` if the copy must differ.\n\nThe full map is on the [React page](./react).\n\nManual list: `<UI.Messages>{(messages) => <span>{messages().length}</span>}</UI.Messages>`.\n\nPass `props.chat`, `props.part`, and `props.Parts` without destructure.\n\n## Render markdown\n\nModel replies arrive as markdown. `TextPart` from `@tanstack/ai-solid/ui` renders it with [TanStack Markdown](https://tanstack.com/markdown). By default, raw HTML is escaped and executable URLs are removed.\n\n```tsx\nimport { TextPart } from '@tanstack/ai-solid/ui'\n\nexport function Reply(props: { content: string }) {\n  return <TextPart content={props.content} />\n}\n```\n\nFenced code stays plain until you pass a `highlighter`. Build one with TanStack Highlight: [Highlight markdown code](./markdown). A custom `highlighter` returns trusted HTML. Use `createTanStackMarkdownHighlighter`, or another highlighter that escapes source text.\n\n- `highlighter`: a synchronous `CodeHighlighter`.\n- `extensions`: extra TanStack Markdown extensions. The streaming extension is always on.\n\nIf you still pass `remarkPlugins`, `rehypePlugins`, `disableDefaultPlugins`, or `components`, see [TextPart markdown](../migration/text-part-markdown).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Solid Chat UI\nid: typed-headless-ui-solid\norder: 2\ndescription: \"Build a typed, headless Solid chat UI with createChatHook. Accessors stay tracked.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - createChatHook\n  - solid\n  - headless ui\n  - ToolProps\n---\n\nInstall `@tanstack/ai-solid`. Import the UI factory from `@tanstack/ai-solid/ui`. Call `createChatHook({ options, ...components })` once at module scope. Your app calls `useAppChat()` to create the instance. Render `<chat.AppChat />`. Do not destructure reactive props.\n\n> **Deprecated.** Do not install `@tanstack/ai-solid-ui`. That package re-exports this subpath until 1.0.0. See [Chat UI packages](../migration/create-ui).\n\nThe factory needs a `toolsComponents` entry for every tool name in `chatOptions`. It also needs an `interruptsComponents.generic` entry for every interrupt id. `generic.fallback` is optional. Widgets go in `components`, `partsComponents`, `toolsComponents`, and `interruptsComponents`, the same way Form and Table register components.\n\nThe server route matches the [React page](./react). Use `gpt-5.6` on the OpenAI text adapter.\n\nThe [chat UI recipes](./recipes/index) show the same option groups one at a time. The code there is React, and the shape carries over.\n\n## Client\n\n```tsx\nimport { createSignal } from 'solid-js'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-solid/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat, useChatContext } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n  layout: (props) => (\n    <>\n      <props.Messages />\n      <props.Interrupts />\n      <props.Queue />\n      <props.Input />\n    </>\n  ),\n  input: () => {\n    const chat = useChatContext()\n    const [draft, setDraft] = createSignal('')\n    return (\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault()\n          void chat.sendMessage(draft())\n          setDraft('')\n        }}\n      >\n        <input onInput={(event) => setDraft(event.currentTarget.value)} value={draft()} />\n        <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n      </form>\n    )\n  },\n  message: (props) => <article><props.Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: {\n  fallback: (props) => <span>{props.part.type}</span>,\n  },\n  toolsComponents: {\n  getWeather: (props) => <strong>{props.part.input?.city}</strong>,\n  },\n})\n\nexport function Support() {\n  const chat = useAppChat({ threadId: 'support-1' })\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}\n```\n\n`layout` receives `props.Messages`, `props.Interrupts`, and `props.Input` as components. `Input` is only present when the config registers an `input`.\n\n> **List `input` before `layout`.** An inline `function` expression written *after* `layout` stops TypeScript inferring that an input is registered, and `Input` goes missing from the layout props. Putting `input` first fixes it, as does an arrow or a named reference. If it slips through, rendering `<props.Input />` without a registered `input` warns once in development.\n\n## Type a component in its own file\n\nUse `ToolProps` the same way as React. Keep the `props` object so Solid can track it.\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\nimport { createChatHook, type ToolProps } from '@tanstack/ai-solid/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nexport function WeatherTool(\n  props: ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'>,\n) {\n  return <strong>{props.part.input?.city}</strong>\n}\n\nexport const { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: (props) => <props.Messages />,\n    message: (props) => <article><props.Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: { fallback: () => null },\n  toolsComponents: { getWeather: WeatherTool },\n})\n```\n\nPart components use `PartProps<typeof chatOptions, 'text'>`. Then `part` is already a text part.\n\nInterrupt components use `InterruptProps<typeof chatOptions, 'choosePlan'>`. Then `interrupt.payload` matches the definition.\n\nMapped components do not receive `chat` as a prop. Call `useChatContext()` when a component needs live chat. That call opts the component into chat updates. Nested children can call it too.\n\n## Read chat from `useChatContext()`\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-solid/ui'\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n}\n\nfunction StatusLine() {\n  const chat = useChatContext()\n  return <p>{chat.messages.length} messages</p>\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat, useChatContext } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: (props) => (\n      <>\n        <StatusLine />\n        <props.Messages />\n      </>\n    ),\n    message: (props) => <article><props.Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: { fallback: () => null },\n})\n\nexport function ChatScreen() {\n  const chat = useAppChat()\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}\n```\n\nCall `useChatContext()` only inside `AppChat` or `Provider`.\n\n## Interrupts\n\nTool approvals sit in the tool when you read `props.interrupt`. Put a component on `interruptsComponents.tools` to send that approval to the list instead. Generic interrupts always sit in the list under `interruptsComponents.generic`: `{ choosePlan, fallback }`. An unbound interrupt uses `fallback`. Branch on `interrupt.kind === 'unbound'` if the copy must differ.\n\nThe full map is on the [React page](./react).\n\nManual list: `<UI.Messages>{(messages) => <span>{messages().length}</span>}</UI.Messages>`.\n\nPass `props.chat`, `props.part`, and `props.Parts` without destructure.\n\n## Render markdown\n\nModel replies arrive as markdown. `TextPart` from `@tanstack/ai-solid/ui` renders it with [TanStack Markdown](https://tanstack.com/markdown). By default, raw HTML is escaped and executable URLs are removed.\n\n```tsx\nimport { TextPart } from '@tanstack/ai-solid/ui'\n\nexport function Reply(props: { content: string }) {\n  return <TextPart content={props.content} />\n}\n```\n\nFenced code stays plain until you pass a `highlighter`. Build one with TanStack Highlight: [Highlight markdown code](./markdown). A custom `highlighter` returns trusted HTML. Use `createTanStackMarkdownHighlighter`, or another highlighter that escapes source text.\n\n- `highlighter`: a synchronous `CodeHighlighter`.\n- `extensions`: extra TanStack Markdown extensions. The streaming extension is always on.\n\nIf you still pass `remarkPlugins`, `rehypePlugins`, `disableDefaultPlugins`, or `components`, see [TextPart markdown](../migration/text-part-markdown).\n"}
